 "notes": "Fermilab Holometer twin 40-m Michelson interferometers, cross-correlated scalar-DM search. Headline = photon coupling Lambda_gamma, Basic Scalar scenario (Fig.2 top-right, gammaC_scalar.pdf), which is identical to the Dilaton/Modulus scenario (same rho=0.4 GeV/cm^3). Red exclusion region boundary (lower edge = smallest excluded 1/Lambda_gamma) extracted from the vector fill via pymupdf get_drawings; axis calibration from frame gridlines (x:10^-15..10^-5 eV, y:10^-25..10^-5 GeV^-1). Converted Lambda_gamma^-1 -> d_e using alpha->alpha(1+phi/Lambda_gamma)=alpha(1+d_e kappa phi), so d_e=(1/Lambda_gamma)/kappa, kappa=sqrt(4pi)/M_Pl, M_Pl=1.22e19 GeV, 1/kappa=3.4416e18. Paper also reports the electron coupling Lambda_e (Fig.2 left; ScalarElectron d_me=(1/Lambda_e)/kappa) equally; photon chosen as main. Relaxion Halo scenario (Fig.2 bottom) assumes enhanced density and is not used. Bathtub curve, min d_e~7e5 near 1e-9 eV. Mass range 1.6e-12..1.0e-7 eV matches abstract.",
